Gabkin <gabriell@programmer.net> writes:
> I found that you cant set autopickup_types to nothing, because if you
> do it takes "nothing" as "everything"!
>
> After a bit of fiddling, the only way I can achieve my means
> (autopickup only the best items) is to set autopickup to something
> like "=" (rings only) and throw in a 
> AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTIONS:">*ring*" (never pick up any rings)
> and use autopickup_exceptions for what I DO want picked up.
> This is an ugly hack, to say the least, and may not be an obvious
> solution to another user.
> 
> Is there a better way to do this?

You should be able to set pickup_types to ']' (you may not be able to
do this from _within_ the game, since it won't be included on any menu
the O command gives you). ] is the symbol for "illegal object", and
thus nothing will match against it.

